--- (logger lost USB at the IIe power cycle; rig cold booted, Pico first, then IIe, PR#5)
# SCOPE ACK timing during PR#5 boot from the board:
#   CH1 J1.10 /WRREQ, CH2 J1.20 ACK, CH3 J1.2 PH0 (REQ); 10x, 2 V/div; GND J1.5
#   trigger CH1 rising 2.52 V, single; 20 us/div, trigger 2 div left of centre (delay -40 us)
#   files: 2026-10-12_ack_wrreq-rise_20us.png, 2026-10-12_ack_ch{1,2,3}_*_20us.csv (500 MSa/s)
# RESULT (computed from CSV, edges at 2.5 V / <1.0 V held 2 us):
#   /WRREQ rise -> ACK low      6.68 us   (card gives up about 105 us after underrun)
#   ACK low     -> REQ low     21.92 us   (card saw ACK, dropped REQ)
#   ACK low     -> ACK high    27.20 us   (reply ready 5 us after REQ low)
#   ACK levels: high 4.72 V, low -0.02 V
#   ACK trace shows crosstalk spikes from WR (J1.18, two pins over) before the ACK.
